-- title:
--   Local description of the replacement in the collar
-- statement:
--   Here `A`, `B` are the perturbations of the hyperbolic metric field and of the second tensor, `sourceSpatial A` is the hyperbolic field plus `A`, and a `SourceCollarAtlas A B ι` is a family of angular coordinate patches of the sphere, covering the sphere, together with a common radius, a compact set of positive-definite angular jets and a common bound giving uniform collar inputs on every patch, with the source fields smooth, the source metric positive definite, the source second tensor symmetric and `physicalDEC` holding for the source data on the tail of each patch beyond that radius. In the situation of a smooth mass aspect $M$ with `bondiCharge M = (m,0)` and symmetric $A,B$ outside `q.radius`, there are $S\ge 1$ and $R_0$ with `q.radius` $<S<R_0$ such that for $R\ge R_0$: every patch is regular and satisfies `physicalDEC` on the collar $R\le y_0\le 3R$, and for every $x$ with $R\le\|x\|\le 3R$ in the polar cone of patch $i$, the replacement metric and tensor coincide with the collar metric and tensor of patch $i$ in a neighbourhood of $x$.
--
--   `q.replacementMetric f₀ m R` equals `sourceSpatial A` for $\|x\|\le R$, the collar metric of the atlas for $R<\|x\|\le 3R$, and the Cartesian outer metric for $\|x\|>3R$; `q.replacementTensor f₀ m R` is defined the same way. In this statement $M$ is a smooth function on $S^2$ with `q.HasMassAspect M`, and $f_0=$ `heatDatum M hM`, the function $M/4$. In this statement $M$ is a smooth function on $S^2$ with `q.HasMassAspect M`, and $f_0=$ `heatDatum M hM`, the function $M/4$.
--
--   **Formal statement.** In the scope of the preamble:
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem SourceCollarAtlas.replacement_localization {A B : SpatialTensor} {ι : Type*}
--       (q : SourceCollarAtlas A B ι) {M : Sphere → ℝ} (hM : SmoothSphere M)
--       (hm : q.HasMassAspect M) (m : ℝ) (hc : bondiCharge M = (m,0))
--       (hA : ∀ x, q.radius < ‖x‖ → ∀ v w, A x v w = A x w v)
--       (hB : ∀ x, q.radius < ‖x‖ → ∀ v w, B x v w = B x w v) :
--       ∃ S R₀ : ℝ, 1 ≤ S ∧ q.radius < S ∧ S < R₀ ∧ ∀ R ≥ R₀,
--         (∀ i y, R ≤ y 0 → y 0 ≤ 3*R → angularProjection y ∈ (q.patch i).region →
--           PhysicalRegularAt (physicalCollarMetric R (sourceCollarData (q.patch i).fields.logFields))
--             (physicalCollarTensor R (sourceCollarData (q.patch i).fields.logFields)) y ∧
--           physicalDEC (physicalCollarMetric R (sourceCollarData (q.patch i).fields.logFields))
--             (physicalCollarTensor R (sourceCollarData (q.patch i).fields.logFields))
--             (physicalCollarFrame R (sourceCollarData (q.patch i).fields.logFields)) y) ∧
--         ∀ i x, R ≤ ‖x‖ → ‖x‖ ≤ 3*R → x ∈ polarCone (q.patch i).patch (q.patch i).region →
--           ∀ᶠ z in 𝓝 x,
--             q.replacementMetric (heatDatum M hM) m R z = (q.patch i).metric R z ∧
--             q.replacementTensor (heatDatum M hM) m R z = (q.patch i).tensor R z
--   ```
--
--   **Formalization Note** The statement is verbatim from `lean/OAI/Geometry/Relativity/CKS/TailEnergy.lean`, lines 3040-3082, in OpenAI's `openai/math` at commit `adc7f12` (Apache-2.0), formalizing part of the construction in the preprint *Area-controlled end replacement and the Bondi–Penrose inequality in the CKS class* (OpenAI, September 27, 2026). It is a supporting lemma for `OAI.CKSSourceExterior.area_controlled_end_replacement`. The definitions it mentions are those of `Definitions.Def_CKSBondiPenrose` and `Definitions.Def_CKSEndReplacementSupport`.
